# The MCP server of a published docs site answers its liveness probe and lists and calls its tools.
# Ported from synthetics/journeys/mcp-server.journey.ts. {{host}} is the site's origin, such as https://www.elastic.co.
# The POSTs only read: they list tools and run a search. The old journey also checked the body for "search_docs" and
# for a JSON-RPC "result"; MCP answers with text/event-stream, which `@expect json` does not read, so those two checks
# wait for a body directive in Nullean.Snapshots.

### MCP liveness endpoint returns 200
# @expect status 200
GET {{host}}/docs/_mcp/alive

### MCP lists its tools
# @readonly
# @expect status 200
# @expect header content-type ~ event-stream
POST {{host}}/docs/_mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list", "params": {}}

### MCP search_docs returns a response
# @readonly
# @expect status 200
# @expect header content-type ~ event-stream
POST {{host}}/docs/_mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "method": "tools/call", "params": {"name": "search_docs", "arguments": {"query": "elasticsearch"}}}
